From: Haldexx
Subject: [PATCH] overlay: enable SIM hotswap

config_hotswapCapable defaults to false, so removing or inserting a SIM while
powered on shows a "reboot required" prompt instead of being handled live. The
Shannon modem reports the SIM card-state change (which drives onIccSwap), so set
config_hotswapCapable=true in the common overlay to handle the swap without a
reboot on every noblelte variant.

---
 overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
--- a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
@@ -950,4 +950,8 @@
          manager will disable alpha trasformation in animations where not
          strictly needed. -->
     <bool name="config_sf_limitedAlpha">true</bool>
+
+    <!-- SIM hotswap: the Shannon modem reports SIM insert/remove, so handle a card swap
+         live (no "reboot required" prompt). -->
+    <bool name="config_hotswapCapable">true</bool>
 </resources>
-- 
2.43.0

